   I have encountered a similar problem: I was praying once and was
   crowned by my god "Hand of Elbereth" (I'm playing a Lawful priest
   character). 700 turns later I prayed again, and my god suddenly was
   displeased with me. I was fairly certain I had done nothing to
   displease him, but to be sure, I quit and restored my save file
   (I'm playing on a PC). I made sure I did nothing that could
   reasonably upset my god, STILL he was displeased with me.

   Do you have to sacrifice something after receiving a gift or
   something like that in NH3.1? How can you tell if your god is
   pleased/displeased whith you? When you quit, it isn't listed in the
   intrinsics list...

1.  If your god gives you something, it's as though you have prayed.
That is, you have to wait or sacrifice before you pray again.

2.  If you are crowned hand of Elbereth (or equivalent for
neutrals/chaotics) item 1 applies, *and* your prayer timeout (i.e. the
interval between "safe" prayers) just went up significantly.  In other
words, you can't pray for food any more.

3.  Killing the wizard bumps up the prayer timeout again.

